  "lit_ht_like_description": "lit_no_ht removes exactly the 9 LIT regulons in data/r2/tables/lit_ht_like_regulons.csv: 5 named high-throughput-like regulons (PAZAR HIF1A; ORegAnno CTCF, YY1, STAT1, GATA2; decision log item 4; named during the first verification partly from ORegAnno's 23% overlap with the held-out ENCODE tags, disclosed) and 4 further regulons with > 500 targets (ExTRI SP1, TP53 [text-mined: large, not high-throughput]; TRED MYC, E2F1; rule added 2026-10-07). It does not remove FANTOM4, the other ORegAnno regulons, NFIRegulomeDB (LIT_other) or HTRIdb; these are removed in lit_no_chipderived.",
  "lit_no_chipderived_drop": [
    "FANTOM4",
    "HTRIdb",
    "ORegAnno",
    "LIT_other"
  ],
  "lit_no_chipderived_description": "lit_no_chipderived removes the whole held-in LIT sources FANTOM4, HTRIdb, ORegAnno, LIT_other (PRESPECIFIED['lit_no_chipderived_drop']; decision log item 9): every held-in literature source that may contain records derived from binding experiments (FANTOM4, HTRIdb incl. its CollecTRI copy, ORegAnno, and LIT_other = DoRothEA-reviews + the 7 non-duplicate NFIRegulomeDB edges); the curated conditioning set is recomputed without them.",
